1
00:00:19,553 --> 00:00:23,193
(The event venue in Dongdaemun where My Star is waiting)

2
00:00:24,293 --> 00:00:26,332
(It's packed with reporters.)

3
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:29,363
(This is the press conference for "The Scandal.")

4
00:00:33,003 --> 00:00:36,403
(He's handling his schedule without the secretaries.)

5
00:00:37,043 --> 00:00:40,613
(Ji Chang Wook, today's My Star)

6
00:00:41,683 --> 00:00:45,253
(The actress joining him for the event is Son Ye Jin.)

7
00:00:45,813 --> 00:00:48,153
(Actress Nana is also here!)

8
00:00:49,083 --> 00:00:52,352
(My Star summoned the secretaries for this important occasion.)

9
00:00:52,353 --> 00:00:53,752
Well...

10
00:00:53,753 --> 00:00:55,092
This is...

11
00:00:55,093 --> 00:00:56,222
my second time.

12
00:00:56,223 --> 00:00:57,862
This is my second time.

13
00:00:57,863 --> 00:01:00,793
So I've gotten closer to them.

14
00:01:01,263 --> 00:01:02,863
We've built a bond.

15
00:01:03,303 --> 00:01:05,172
- Is this okay?
- What?

16
00:01:05,173 --> 00:01:08,972
(Last November, Chang Wook appeared on the show as My Star.)

17
00:01:08,973 --> 00:01:11,443
You can drive if this is uncomfortable for you, Chang Wook.

18
00:01:11,843 --> 00:01:13,972
(When he suggested going to a bakery)

19
00:01:13,973 --> 00:01:15,182
It's near Gangnam-gu Office.

20
00:01:15,183 --> 00:01:16,382
- Gosh, that's too far.
- That's too far.

21
00:01:16,383 --> 00:01:17,413
- Sorry?
- That's too far.

22
00:01:18,083 --> 00:01:20,183
- Is Gangnam-gu Office...
- Are you perplexed?

23
00:01:20,253 --> 00:01:22,522
We're running late...

24
00:01:22,523 --> 00:01:23,783
because of the traffic jam.

25
00:01:25,123 --> 00:01:27,422
(They were even late.)

26
00:01:27,423 --> 00:01:28,793
Did I...

27
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:31,392
get to do anything...

28
00:01:31,393 --> 00:01:32,593
I wanted to do today?

29
00:01:34,863 --> 00:01:37,162
(My Star has been through a tough experience.)

30
00:01:37,163 --> 00:01:38,733
(Worked up)

31
00:01:39,633 --> 00:01:40,833
We got closer...

32
00:01:40,973 --> 00:01:42,702
and built a bond.

33
00:01:42,703 --> 00:01:45,112
I'm sure we'll have better teamwork this time.

34
00:01:45,113 --> 00:01:46,772
That's what I'm expecting.

35
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:48,082
And today,

36
00:01:48,083 --> 00:01:49,812
we have a press conference.

37
00:01:49,813 --> 00:01:51,283
It's a public event,

38
00:01:51,583 --> 00:01:53,652
so I'm sure...

39
00:01:53,653 --> 00:01:56,783
they'll behave appropriately...

40
00:01:56,823 --> 00:01:59,553
for the occasion.

41
00:02:02,823 --> 00:02:06,633
(A sound effect worthy of a global streaming platform)

42
00:02:08,463 --> 00:02:09,702
(Staggering)

43
00:02:09,703 --> 00:02:11,103
Why did you get out like that?

44
00:02:11,703 --> 00:02:13,103
Why did you get out like that?

45
00:02:13,333 --> 00:02:15,172
(Anyone would think he's a local cab driver.)

46
00:02:15,173 --> 00:02:17,003
Why did you leave your buttons undone?

47
00:02:22,083 --> 00:02:24,453
(He shamelessly uses someone else's vehicle.)

48
00:02:25,783 --> 00:02:27,612
It's hot. Let's go somewhere in the shade.

49
00:02:27,613 --> 00:02:28,823
It's hot.

50
00:02:29,223 --> 00:02:30,522
It'll burn my skin.

51
00:02:30,523 --> 00:02:31,723
(The sun seems to feel especially hot to Driver Kim.)

52
00:02:32,293 --> 00:02:36,292
(His soulmate arrives shortly afterward.)

53
00:02:36,293 --> 00:02:37,393
Hi.

54
00:02:37,963 --> 00:02:39,662
I thought you were a manager or something.

55
00:02:39,663 --> 00:02:41,462
(I thought you were a manager or something.)

56
00:02:41,463 --> 00:02:43,832
Welcome, Young Master.

57
00:02:43,833 --> 00:02:44,833
(His dimples show when he sees his older bestie's outfit.)

58
00:02:46,273 --> 00:02:48,442
You said you wouldn't wear a blazer. Why are you wearing it?

59
00:02:48,443 --> 00:02:50,042
(Seo Jin is wearing a neat suit.)

60
00:02:50,043 --> 00:02:52,172
You said you wouldn't wear it, but here you are.

61
00:02:52,173 --> 00:02:53,273
I knew it.

62
00:02:56,513 --> 00:03:00,212
(The two men in suits enter the venue.)

63
00:03:00,213 --> 00:03:04,083
(Dashing)

64
00:03:04,123 --> 00:03:05,253
This way?

65
00:03:05,993 --> 00:03:07,152
Is the global streaming service hosting this event?

66
00:03:07,153 --> 00:03:08,463
Yes.

67
00:03:09,493 --> 00:03:11,533
(If so...)

68
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:13,992
(He quickly checks his appearance...)

69
00:03:13,993 --> 00:03:15,763
(to make sure he looks good on a global stage.)

70
00:03:16,533 --> 00:03:17,602
(He's even wearing a name tag from the global OTT platform.)

71
00:03:17,603 --> 00:03:18,733
You guys look like agents.

72
00:03:20,403 --> 00:03:21,442
Hello.

73
00:03:21,443 --> 00:03:24,943
(They head over to meet My Star, looking classy.)

74
00:03:28,683 --> 00:03:29,713
Hello.

75
00:03:30,343 --> 00:03:31,453
Hello.

76
00:03:32,653 --> 00:03:33,783
Hello.

77
00:03:34,253 --> 00:03:35,752
Is he the manager we saw last time?

78
00:03:35,753 --> 00:03:36,922
- I don't know.
- Maybe not?

79
00:03:36,923 --> 00:03:38,153
You must be his new manager.

80
00:03:38,353 --> 00:03:39,952
- No, we met last time.
- Are you the same manager?

81
00:03:39,953 --> 00:03:41,622
- Yes.
- Why do you look different today?

82
00:03:41,623 --> 00:03:43,663
- Right. It's the suit.
- Please take a seat here.

83
00:03:43,863 --> 00:03:44,863
- Hello.
- Hello.

84
00:03:44,864 --> 00:03:47,632
(They met the manager last season.)

85
00:03:47,633 --> 00:03:50,202
(1 year ago, now)

86
00:03:50,203 --> 00:03:53,172
(His style has changed quite a lot since they last saw him.)

87
00:03:53,173 --> 00:03:54,302
- Are you the same manager?
- Yes.

88
00:03:54,303 --> 00:03:55,642
Why do you look different today?

89
00:03:55,643 --> 00:03:57,102
Right. It's the suit.

90
00:03:57,103 --> 00:03:58,713
- Please take a seat here.
- Here?

91
00:03:59,213 --> 00:04:01,343
You look like a different person.

92
00:04:02,243 --> 00:04:04,012
Today is the press conference...

93
00:04:04,013 --> 00:04:07,083
for the OTT original series "The Scandal."

94
00:04:07,153 --> 00:04:09,253
This is his second time appearing on My Genie Secretary.

95
00:04:09,453 --> 00:04:10,883
Please take good care of him.

96
00:04:11,453 --> 00:04:13,352
It'll be released on September 18.

97
00:04:13,353 --> 00:04:14,392
It's nice to meet you.

98
00:04:14,393 --> 00:04:16,893
It sounds like you memorized those lines.

99
00:04:16,993 --> 00:04:18,092
Yes, I did.

100
00:04:18,093 --> 00:04:19,193
(He got caught.)

101
00:04:20,933 --> 00:04:22,732
I suggested...

102
00:04:22,733 --> 00:04:26,902
you wear suits.

103
00:04:26,903 --> 00:04:29,173
- Was that you?
- Yes.

104
00:04:29,473 --> 00:04:31,372
(I didn't need to wear a suit after all.)

105
00:04:31,373 --> 00:04:32,872
You looked better in the outfit...

106
00:04:32,873 --> 00:04:34,372
- you wore last time.
- Right.

107
00:04:34,373 --> 00:04:36,182
- You look awkward.
- Yes.

108
00:04:36,183 --> 00:04:37,813
(They tease him right away since they've met before.)

109
00:04:37,913 --> 00:04:39,412
You look like you're wearing someone else's clothes.

110
00:04:39,413 --> 00:04:40,913
- You can't even button it.
- Hey.

111
00:04:41,053 --> 00:04:42,753
That button is about to pop off.

112
00:04:43,883 --> 00:04:45,923
Try buttoning it.

113
00:04:46,553 --> 00:04:48,562
- This is...
- Did you try to lose weight or...

114
00:04:48,563 --> 00:04:49,762
(It's just cruel to the button.)

115
00:04:49,763 --> 00:04:51,333
That button might hit us in the eye.

116
00:04:52,433 --> 00:04:54,803
(Their antics get him dizzy.)

117
00:04:54,903 --> 00:04:56,462
I'll tell Chang Wook...

118
00:04:56,463 --> 00:04:58,003
- to buy you a suit.
- No, it's okay.

119
00:04:58,533 --> 00:04:59,802
Don't take it too far.

120
00:04:59,803 --> 00:05:01,003
(Laughing)

121
00:05:01,743 --> 00:05:04,872
This is today's schedule and the company card.

122
00:05:04,873 --> 00:05:06,273
Please take a look.

123
00:05:06,373 --> 00:05:07,812
Please brief him...

124
00:05:07,813 --> 00:05:11,113
on today's schedule when you meet him.

125
00:05:11,553 --> 00:05:14,382
(My Star's Schedule, Time: 9:30am to 5pm, Location: Press Conference)

126
00:05:14,383 --> 00:05:15,682
(His schedule is packed...)

127
00:05:15,683 --> 00:05:17,782
(with promotional events until the evening.)

128
00:05:17,783 --> 00:05:19,953
(The project he'll be presenting this time is...)

129
00:05:20,553 --> 00:05:23,662
Actually, I have a favour to ask...

130
00:05:23,663 --> 00:05:26,433
(For My Star's impressive acting...)

131
00:05:26,633 --> 00:05:27,793
A favour?

132
00:05:29,303 --> 00:05:32,033
(and the cast's transformations, it's already been making headlines.)

133
00:05:33,203 --> 00:05:35,172
(The most highly anticipated release of the second half of the year)

134
00:05:35,173 --> 00:05:37,102
(The temptation of three people who dare to cross the line)

135
00:05:37,103 --> 00:05:39,313
("The Scandal")

136
00:05:40,243 --> 00:05:42,683
(This time, he's back as the greatest ladies' man in Joseon.)

137
00:05:43,213 --> 00:05:44,312
Are they doing an interview?

138
00:05:44,313 --> 00:05:46,052
- Yes.
- Is it live?

139
00:05:46,053 --> 00:05:49,183
They're in an interview with an international media outlet.

140
00:05:50,253 --> 00:05:52,122
(They're doing a video interview...)

141
00:05:52,123 --> 00:05:54,793
(with an international media outlet in the room right next door.)

142
00:05:55,423 --> 00:05:57,763
It's not morning in South America right now.

143
00:05:58,093 --> 00:06:00,433
It must be evening there.

144
00:06:01,303 --> 00:06:04,732
(The actors are connecting with audiences around the world.)

145
00:06:04,733 --> 00:06:08,302
No one is entirely innocent, and every character is in the gray area.

146
00:06:08,303 --> 00:06:11,773
I'd like you to defend your characters.

147
00:06:14,343 --> 00:06:17,343
I'm not sure. How should I defend him?

148
00:06:17,743 --> 00:06:18,853
He loved them.

149
00:06:19,213 --> 00:06:21,183
(Laughing)

150
00:06:22,383 --> 00:06:23,852
Love isn't a crime, is it?

151
00:06:23,853 --> 00:06:25,193
(My Star lightens the mood with a playful remark.)

152
00:06:25,353 --> 00:06:28,193
Actually, there's nothing else I can say...

153
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:30,193
to defend him.

154
00:06:30,923 --> 00:06:34,233
The press conference will be starting again shortly.

155
00:06:34,393 --> 00:06:36,162
As you both know,

156
00:06:36,163 --> 00:06:38,803
please keep an eye on the articles and comments on online communities.

157
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:40,933
- Search his name online.
- That's...

158
00:06:41,073 --> 00:06:43,443
And since he'll be using his voice a lot today,

159
00:06:44,043 --> 00:06:45,942
- make sure he has...
- There's a tumbler.

160
00:06:45,943 --> 00:06:47,542
Yes. This tumbler and the things we prepared for him.

161
00:06:47,543 --> 00:06:48,942
Isn't it the same tumbler from last time?

162
00:06:48,943 --> 00:06:51,383
- It is.
- I forgot to take it.

163
00:06:51,513 --> 00:06:53,212
- You left it behind.
- Yes.

164
00:06:53,213 --> 00:06:55,153
(This tumbler is...)

165
00:06:56,523 --> 00:06:59,623
- Thank you, Kwang Kyu.
- I forgot to take it.

166
00:06:59,923 --> 00:07:01,592
Please be mindful.

167
00:07:01,593 --> 00:07:02,922
(A careful request)

168
00:07:02,923 --> 00:07:05,663
I'll be more mindful. Gosh, there's a mosquito.

169
00:07:06,393 --> 00:07:08,402
- My apologies.
- No, it's fine.

170
00:07:08,403 --> 00:07:10,132
I'm sorry. It was my fault.

171
00:07:10,133 --> 00:07:11,303
But he's not going anywhere today.

172
00:07:11,773 --> 00:07:14,073
- He will after it's over.
- He'll stay in the same venue.

173
00:07:14,173 --> 00:07:16,103
These are good for his throat.

174
00:07:16,943 --> 00:07:18,243
- And...
- What are good for his throat?

175
00:07:18,343 --> 00:07:21,613
Honey and effervescent vitamin tablets.

176
00:07:21,743 --> 00:07:23,143
I put these in the bag.

177
00:07:24,013 --> 00:07:27,453
I'd appreciate it if you put them in his tumbler.

178
00:07:27,713 --> 00:07:29,882
I put everything he needs in the bag.

179
00:07:29,883 --> 00:07:31,793
My goodness.

180
00:07:33,893 --> 00:07:37,923
(He couldn't wait and is already sucking on some honey.)

181
00:07:38,593 --> 00:07:40,493
Please take good care of our staff members too.

182
00:07:40,663 --> 00:07:43,433
Make sure to check on the other actors' managers...

183
00:07:43,603 --> 00:07:45,172
Can we go to a buffet and pay with this card?

184
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:46,503
- Do you want to go to a buffet?
- Yes.

185
00:07:46,903 --> 00:07:51,303
(He has a feeling their aftercare service is going to fail too.)

186
00:07:51,643 --> 00:07:54,372
Please make sure Chang Wook gets to do whatever he wants.

187
00:07:54,373 --> 00:07:55,913
When has he ever not gotten to do what he wants?

188
00:07:56,513 --> 00:07:59,053
(His Genie secretaries will do anything this time.)

189
00:07:59,153 --> 00:08:01,983
(Meanwhile, in the interview room)

190
00:08:03,053 --> 00:08:07,622
(My Star is in the middle of an interview.)

191
00:08:07,623 --> 00:08:10,962
The characters' good and evil sides aren't clearly defined.

192
00:08:10,963 --> 00:08:14,463
(Staring)

193
00:08:15,033 --> 00:08:17,203
Did she leave that one strand of hair out on purpose?

194
00:08:18,803 --> 00:08:20,933
(A strand of hair is bothering Seo Jin.)

195
00:08:21,503 --> 00:08:24,643
(His eyes are fixed on someone's hair instead of My Star.)

196
00:08:24,873 --> 00:08:27,343
This is what managers do.

197
00:08:27,443 --> 00:08:29,043
- You should do that too.
- What?

198
00:08:29,183 --> 00:08:30,782
Why? That looks wrong.

199
00:08:30,783 --> 00:08:32,283
- Is that wrong?
- I want to fix it.

200
00:08:32,653 --> 00:08:35,523
You're Chang Wook's manager, but you're more interested in her.

201
00:08:36,123 --> 00:08:37,623
He'll take care of himself.

202
00:08:39,593 --> 00:08:42,693
(I also left a few strands of my hair down.)

203
00:08:43,893 --> 00:08:46,563
(Another secretary is distracted as well.)

204
00:08:47,133 --> 00:08:50,333
I've briefly worked with all of those actors.

205
00:08:50,363 --> 00:08:52,472
- Do you know them all then?
- Of course.

206
00:08:52,473 --> 00:08:53,603
What project did you work on with Ye Jin?

207
00:08:54,033 --> 00:08:56,042
A drama called "Blood and Ties."

208
00:08:56,043 --> 00:08:58,743
- Isn't it a movie? Is it a drama?
- It's a movie.

209
00:08:58,973 --> 00:09:00,113
You said it was a drama.

210
00:09:01,013 --> 00:09:02,383
Were you in the same scene as her?

211
00:09:02,943 --> 00:09:04,113
Yes, I was.

212
00:09:04,343 --> 00:09:05,913
- So you worked with everyone.
- Right.

213
00:09:06,653 --> 00:09:07,753
Did you work with Nana as well?

214
00:09:08,253 --> 00:09:09,783
There was a drama called "Genesis,"

215
00:09:09,953 --> 00:09:12,922
which was cancelled halfway through.

216
00:09:12,923 --> 00:09:14,623
(He met Nana through a drama.)

217
00:09:15,363 --> 00:09:18,633
(Kwang Kyu has worked with all three actors before.)

218
00:09:19,063 --> 00:09:20,963
I'm curious.

219
00:09:21,433 --> 00:09:23,133
Will Nana recognise me?

220
00:09:24,133 --> 00:09:26,232
She would know who you are,

221
00:09:26,233 --> 00:09:27,672
but I'm not sure if she remembers working with you.

222
00:09:27,673 --> 00:09:29,342
Is that what you want to know?

223
00:09:29,343 --> 00:09:31,742
Because we only worked together briefly.

224
00:09:31,743 --> 00:09:32,772
She might not remember then.

225
00:09:32,773 --> 00:09:34,173
- Were you in the same scene as her?
- What?

226
00:09:34,313 --> 00:09:36,343
- Were you in the same scene as her?
- Of course.

227
00:09:36,913 --> 00:09:40,653
When I fell,

228
00:09:42,883 --> 00:09:44,323
she helped me up.

229
00:09:45,253 --> 00:09:46,622
She was so kind.

230
00:09:46,623 --> 00:09:48,392
(Kwang Kyu has fond memories of her.)

231
00:09:48,393 --> 00:09:52,193
(Looking at Nana only)

232
00:09:52,263 --> 00:09:53,632
Thank you.

233
00:09:53,633 --> 00:09:55,833
(The interview is over.)

234
00:09:56,033 --> 00:09:58,973
(My Star leaves first.)

235
00:10:01,573 --> 00:10:02,573
Chang Wook.

236
00:10:04,243 --> 00:10:05,273
Chang Wook.

237
00:10:05,543 --> 00:10:07,112
(Spotting the secretaries)

238
00:10:07,113 --> 00:10:10,212
Why do you keep calling us?

239
00:10:10,213 --> 00:10:12,212
(They finally met My Star.)

240
00:10:12,213 --> 00:10:13,612
- Did you want to meet us again?
- Yes.

241
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:15,623
- I missed you guys so much.
- Gosh.

242
00:10:15,723 --> 00:10:16,723
- Your suit is amazing.
- Sorry?

243
00:10:16,724 --> 00:10:18,322
- Let me change...
- Sure.

244
00:10:18,323 --> 00:10:19,953
- my pants.
- Sure.

245
00:10:20,393 --> 00:10:22,763
(My Star is getting changed.)

246
00:10:24,163 --> 00:10:27,592
(Nana leaves the interview room.)

247
00:10:27,593 --> 00:10:28,862
Hi.

248
00:10:28,863 --> 00:10:30,863
(That's Nana's voice.)

249
00:10:32,073 --> 00:10:36,003
(Does she remember him?)

250
00:10:37,543 --> 00:10:38,543
Nana.

251
00:10:38,544 --> 00:10:41,073
(Nana)

252
00:10:42,143 --> 00:10:43,583
- Hello.
- Hello.

253
00:10:43,813 --> 00:10:44,883
Do you remember me?

254
00:10:45,483 --> 00:10:47,053
- Of course, I do.
- You do?

255
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:48,853
You know the drama aired, right?

256
00:10:48,923 --> 00:10:51,352
- It aired.
- I didn't know.

257
00:10:51,353 --> 00:10:53,853
I didn't even get paid.

258
00:10:54,493 --> 00:10:57,463
I only found out about it recently.

259
00:10:57,763 --> 00:10:59,492
(He's a lot happier to see Nana than My Star.)

260
00:10:59,493 --> 00:11:01,363
- Weren't you hurt at the time?
- No, I wasn't.

261
00:11:01,493 --> 00:11:02,562
You weren't?

262
00:11:02,563 --> 00:11:04,933
