- Yes.

510
00:20:43,813 --> 00:20:45,282
I'm quite sensitive.

511
00:20:45,283 --> 00:20:46,513
(Are they not paying attention again?)

512
00:20:47,183 --> 00:20:49,353
(Glancing at Seo Jin)

513
00:20:50,083 --> 00:20:52,083
(Glancing at Ye Jin)

514
00:20:53,323 --> 00:20:57,423
(My Star wants the secretaries' attention.)

515
00:20:58,763 --> 00:21:00,463
(Oh, right.)

516
00:21:01,263 --> 00:21:02,432
How is Kyung Soo doing?

517
00:21:02,433 --> 00:21:04,232
- Kyung Soo? I haven't seen him...
- You haven't seen him?

518
00:21:04,233 --> 00:21:05,932
- for a very long time. Yes.
- Is that so?

519
00:21:05,933 --> 00:21:08,172
You work all the time. How are you supposed to meet anyone?

520
00:21:08,173 --> 00:21:09,373
- I know.
- Right?

521
00:21:09,673 --> 00:21:11,572
We saw Kyung Soo last time. I guess that was the last time he saw him.

522
00:21:11,573 --> 00:21:12,573
Really?

523
00:21:12,574 --> 00:21:13,772
You were promoting together.

524
00:21:13,773 --> 00:21:15,513
You're right.

525
00:21:15,743 --> 00:21:17,482
After it aired,

526
00:21:17,483 --> 00:21:19,653
I started shooting another drama.

527
00:21:20,683 --> 00:21:21,683
So I haven't seen him for a very long time.

528
00:21:21,684 --> 00:21:23,383
These days,

529
00:21:23,683 --> 00:21:25,153
I haven't met anyone.

530
00:21:25,753 --> 00:21:27,652
When work is over,

531
00:21:27,653 --> 00:21:30,462
- You need to rest.
- I'm too busy resting at home.

532
00:21:30,463 --> 00:21:32,062
I either work or stay at home.

533
00:21:32,063 --> 00:21:34,662
I've lost touch with everyone.

534
00:21:34,663 --> 00:21:35,862
- I've become a bit of a loner.
- Yes.

535
00:21:35,863 --> 00:21:38,332
(Ji Chang Wook, 39 years old, My Star, a loner)

536
00:21:38,333 --> 00:21:39,873
- It's because you always work.
- Yes.

537
00:21:40,733 --> 00:21:42,903
No one calls me anymore.

538
00:21:44,573 --> 00:21:46,442
(Teary-eyed)

539
00:21:46,443 --> 00:21:48,012
When you take on a year-long project,

540
00:21:48,013 --> 00:21:49,612
your social life basically comes to an end.

541
00:21:49,613 --> 00:21:50,713
That's so true.

542
00:21:51,713 --> 00:21:54,113
It's embarrassing now.

543
00:21:54,613 --> 00:21:55,653
Why?

544
00:21:56,483 --> 00:21:57,982
If someone calls...

545
00:21:57,983 --> 00:22:00,692
- And they ask you to meet up?
- and asks to meet up,

546
00:22:00,693 --> 00:22:01,922
I feel bad having to turn them down...

547
00:22:01,923 --> 00:22:04,022
- because I have a shoot.
- Is it easier...

548
00:22:04,023 --> 00:22:05,893
- if they don't call you at all?
- Yes.

549
00:22:06,333 --> 00:22:08,593
That's why I didn't contact you. I didn't want you to feel bad.

550
00:22:09,533 --> 00:22:11,462
(That's a lame excuse.)

551
00:22:11,463 --> 00:22:13,772
- But we met today.
- Yes.

552
00:22:13,773 --> 00:22:15,433
- This is the best way to meet up.
- Yes.

553
00:22:15,973 --> 00:22:17,942
We'll begin today's press conference for "The Scandal..."

554
00:22:17,943 --> 00:22:20,973
with a photo call.

555
00:22:21,573 --> 00:22:25,213
Please welcome Nana to the stage, who plays Hui Yeon.

556
00:22:25,513 --> 00:22:27,212
(The photo call begins with Nana.)

557
00:22:27,213 --> 00:22:29,322
Nana takes on her first historical drama...

558
00:22:29,323 --> 00:22:31,523
with "The Scandal," making a new transformation.

559
00:22:31,783 --> 00:22:32,892
Please look forward to it...

560
00:22:32,893 --> 00:22:34,022
(Despite saying she's nervous, she poses with ease.)

561
00:22:34,023 --> 00:22:35,522
and show her lots of love.

562
00:22:35,523 --> 00:22:37,722
- Mr. Ji.
- Yes.

563
00:22:37,723 --> 00:22:40,992
Please go on stage when Nana comes down.

564
00:22:40,993 --> 00:22:42,463
Show her lots of love.

565
00:22:43,663 --> 00:22:44,732
Please stand here.

566
00:22:44,733 --> 00:22:45,932
(Holding hands)

567
00:22:45,933 --> 00:22:48,532
(My Star is a little nervous.)

568
00:22:48,533 --> 00:22:50,573
Has it already been this long?

569
00:22:50,603 --> 00:22:51,643
- I know.
- Gosh.

570
00:22:52,073 --> 00:22:53,872
- Look toward the center.
- My gosh.

571
00:22:53,873 --> 00:22:55,612
(Seo Jin is watching My Star who feels nervous.)

572
00:22:55,613 --> 00:22:57,643
We filmed the drama in the middle of summer last year.

573
00:22:58,743 --> 00:23:01,853
(Actually, he's watching Ye Jin.)

574
00:23:04,953 --> 00:23:06,552
You don't have to look in the mirror. You look pretty.

575
00:23:06,553 --> 00:23:08,962
You look pretty. Stop looking in the mirror.

576
00:23:08,963 --> 00:23:10,922
- Why do you say that?
- It's because you look pretty.

577
00:23:10,923 --> 00:23:11,963
(He successfully grabbed her attention.)

578
00:23:12,533 --> 00:23:13,692
(His dimples deepen.)

579
00:23:13,693 --> 00:23:14,733
I mean...

580
00:23:15,533 --> 00:23:17,462
Do you want some honey?

581
00:23:17,463 --> 00:23:20,832
(Do you want some honey?)

582
00:23:20,833 --> 00:23:22,542
- I'm fine.
- Honey? It's good for your throat.

583
00:23:22,543 --> 00:23:24,472
If I eat honey now,

584
00:23:24,473 --> 00:23:26,012
my mouth might feel sticky during the press conference.

585
00:23:26,013 --> 00:23:27,013
Is that so?

586
00:23:28,043 --> 00:23:29,142
It surprised me...

587
00:23:29,143 --> 00:23:32,913
when he talked to Ye Jin.

588
00:23:33,283 --> 00:23:34,713
He doesn't usually do that.

589
00:23:35,113 --> 00:23:37,522
She kept coughing. That's why.

590
00:23:37,523 --> 00:23:39,122
(A lame excuse)

591
00:23:39,123 --> 00:23:41,592
She looked fine to me.

592
00:23:41,593 --> 00:23:43,123
She kept coughing.

593
00:23:43,623 --> 00:23:45,463
She kept coughing next to me.

594
00:23:45,833 --> 00:23:47,133
We'll check the footage.

595
00:23:47,463 --> 00:23:49,503
Go on. I talked to her because she kept coughing.

596
00:23:50,033 --> 00:23:53,133
(We checked the footage, and she didn't cough.)

597
00:23:53,373 --> 00:23:55,102
How about a strand of hair you were talking about?

598
00:23:55,103 --> 00:23:56,642
- I think she did that on purpose.
- I did that on purpose.

599
00:23:56,643 --> 00:23:57,702
(I left that on purpose.)

600
00:23:57,703 --> 00:23:58,742
(I see.)

601
00:23:58,743 --> 00:23:59,913
Okay.

602
00:24:00,173 --> 00:24:02,542
(They leave My Star to his nerves...)

603
00:24:02,543 --> 00:24:07,412
(and keep chatting.)

604
00:24:07,413 --> 00:24:08,553
Why are you so good at golf?

605
00:24:08,853 --> 00:24:10,383
- Excuse me?
- You're good at golf.

606
00:24:10,623 --> 00:24:12,593
- You saw the YouTube video?
- Yes.

607
00:24:12,753 --> 00:24:14,852
I practised.

608
00:24:14,853 --> 00:24:16,922
You're quite good.

609
00:24:16,923 --> 00:24:18,362
Do you shoot in the 80s?

610
00:24:18,363 --> 00:24:19,363
(No)

611
00:24:19,364 --> 00:24:21,232
- No.
- You shoot in the 100s, right?

612
00:24:21,233 --> 00:24:22,363
I do.

613
00:24:22,633 --> 00:24:23,733
You're good.

614
00:24:24,363 --> 00:24:25,532
I just have good form.

615
00:24:25,533 --> 00:24:27,273
Your form looks good.

616
00:24:27,573 --> 00:24:29,872
Is your husband still a single-digit handicap?

617
00:24:29,873 --> 00:24:31,073
- Yes.
- Is he?

618
00:24:31,103 --> 00:24:33,072
- He hasn't played golf for a while.
- Is that so?

619
00:24:33,073 --> 00:24:34,643
But he's good.

620
00:24:34,673 --> 00:24:36,283
- That's what I heard.
- He's good.

621
00:24:36,543 --> 00:24:39,182
I heard it from his friends that he's good...

622
00:24:39,183 --> 00:24:41,083
because they are my juniors.

623
00:24:42,013 --> 00:24:45,822
Some of her husband's friends...

624
00:24:45,823 --> 00:24:47,823
are my juniors.

625
00:24:48,323 --> 00:24:51,493
Ye Jin is good at golf. I saw her video on YouTube.

626
00:24:51,793 --> 00:24:54,263
That's why I asked.

627
00:24:54,963 --> 00:24:58,103
Have you watched Chang Wook's video on YouTube recently?

628
00:24:58,633 --> 00:24:59,672
Was he on YouTube?

629
00:24:59,673 --> 00:25:02,702
(He had no idea.)

630
00:25:02,703 --> 00:25:04,302
Thank you. I'll see you later.

631
00:25:04,303 --> 00:25:05,342
(Glancing)

632
00:25:05,343 --> 00:25:06,512
Please go back the way you came.

633
00:25:06,513 --> 00:25:10,783
Please welcome Ji Chang Wook who played Cho Won.

634
00:25:11,843 --> 00:25:14,952
He'll show a new side of himself...

635
00:25:14,953 --> 00:25:18,383
as Joseon's greatest ladies' man in "The Scandal."

636
00:25:19,023 --> 00:25:21,092
Everyone looks amazing today.

637
00:25:21,093 --> 00:25:22,093
(Charismatic)

638
00:25:22,094 --> 00:25:26,092
Yes. You're Joseon's greatest ladies' man.

639
00:25:26,093 --> 00:25:27,993
Can you show us a heart?

640
00:25:29,303 --> 00:25:30,602
That's what I'm talking about.

641
00:25:30,603 --> 00:25:32,473
Look to your left.

642
00:25:33,173 --> 00:25:35,373
Why does he never stop working?

643
00:25:35,573 --> 00:25:36,803
- Who?
- Chang Wook.

644
00:25:38,073 --> 00:25:40,013
All right. Great.

645
00:25:40,173 --> 00:25:43,113
The crew has perfect teamwork.

646
00:25:43,243 --> 00:25:45,682
Let's wrap up the photo call.

647
00:25:45,683 --> 00:25:46,853
Thank you.

648
00:25:49,453 --> 00:25:55,423
(A short break before the question-and-answer session)

649
00:25:56,263 --> 00:25:57,723
(Picking up)

650
00:26:00,063 --> 00:26:02,092
(Kwang Kyu goes straight to My Star to give him a tumbler.)

651
00:26:02,093 --> 00:26:04,263
(Thank you.)

652
00:26:04,533 --> 00:26:07,432
(He even fans him with a portable fan.)

653
00:26:07,433 --> 00:26:08,503
How come this is so strong?

654
00:26:08,533 --> 00:26:11,043
It's not a portable fan. It's an air gun.

655
00:26:11,143 --> 00:26:12,672
(An air gun for My Star)

656
00:26:12,673 --> 00:26:13,742
It sounds like an airplane.

657
00:26:13,743 --> 00:26:15,542
I place it here when it gets hot.

658
00:26:15,543 --> 00:26:16,682
(Demonstrating)

659
00:26:16,683 --> 00:26:17,712
It's really strong.

660
00:26:17,713 --> 00:26:19,182
- There's such a thing?
- It's an air gun.

661
00:26:19,183 --> 00:26:20,953
It's like a hair dryer.

662
00:26:21,383 --> 00:26:22,453
It's no joke.

663
00:26:23,183 --> 00:26:28,823
(The 56.5-year-old secretaries discovered modern technology.)

664
00:26:29,763 --> 00:26:31,793
(Wandering around)

665
00:26:33,193 --> 00:26:36,962
(Kwang Kyu heads somewhere with the air gun.)

666
00:26:36,963 --> 00:26:40,573
(He sits next to Nana instead of My Star.)

667
00:26:43,243 --> 00:26:45,302
- Right here.
- Right there. Goodness.

668
00:26:45,303 --> 00:26:48,273
- At the back.
- It's been a while, Nana.

669
00:26:48,313 --> 00:26:50,643
It's been a while, Nana.

670
00:26:51,083 --> 00:26:52,513
- What is he doing?
- Ji Chang Wook.

671
00:26:53,153 --> 00:26:55,153
(Read the room, Kwang Kyu.)

672
00:26:55,383 --> 00:26:57,782
(Unaware of the tension, he's busy taking care of Nana.)

673
00:26:57,783 --> 00:26:59,353
I know, right? It's been a long while.

674
00:26:59,523 --> 00:27:00,793
- I'll head out.
- Okay.

675
00:27:00,853 --> 00:27:01,993
My Star.

676
00:27:02,253 --> 00:27:04,862
My Star.

677
00:27:04,863 --> 00:27:08,292
(She's even taken the title of "My Star.")

678
00:27:08,293 --> 00:27:10,162
Did you know that they kept wandering...

679
00:27:10,163 --> 00:27:12,673
around Son Ye Jin and Nana?

680
00:27:13,133 --> 00:27:14,173
(Exclaiming)

681
00:27:14,403 --> 00:27:16,372
(Worried look)

682
00:27:16,373 --> 00:27:17,572
Actually,

683
00:27:17,573 --> 00:27:18,802
I knew that...

684
00:27:18,803 --> 00:27:20,012
they weren't next to me.

685
00:27:20,013 --> 00:27:22,983
(I know very well that they weren't next to me.)

686
00:27:25,613 --> 00:27:26,782
I'll head out.

687
00:27:26,783 --> 00:27:28,383
(I'll head out.)

688
00:27:28,483 --> 00:27:30,852
(Putting aside his disappointment, he heads into the press conference.)

689
00:27:30,853 --> 00:27:33,193
We'll invite them to the stage.

690
00:27:36,893 --> 00:27:38,792
(My Star gets on the stage first.)

691
00:27:38,793 --> 00:27:40,632
I think it's because of their fancy clothes.

692
00:27:40,633 --> 00:27:43,303
The stage feels like a runway.

693
00:27:43,803 --> 00:27:45,163
Can we enter?

694
00:27:47,373 --> 00:27:53,243
(The secretaries stand by next to the stage.)

695
00:27:53,343 --> 00:27:56,112
Hello, I'm Ji Chang Wook, playing the role of Cho Won.

696
00:27:56,113 --> 00:27:57,242
Nice to meet you.

697
00:27:57,243 --> 00:27:58,483
Nice to meet you.

698
00:27:59,483 --> 00:28:02,013
(Taking a picture of him before he misses it)

699
00:28:03,383 --> 00:28:05,993
(Making sure to zoom in)

700
00:28:07,853 --> 00:28:09,222
Get one on film.

701
00:28:09,223 --> 00:28:10,693
(My Star's request)

702
00:28:10,923 --> 00:28:12,863
(Complying)

703
00:28:14,863 --> 00:28:16,362
- Make sure they all appear.
- I thought it was interesting.

704
00:28:16,363 --> 00:28:17,562
- All of them?
- And...

705
00:28:17,563 --> 00:28:20,272
- Does the title show up as well?
- the work with the director...

706
00:28:20,273 --> 00:28:22,973
- Yes.
- I'm excited to work with him.

707
00:28:25,073 --> 00:28:27,073
You should take it.

708
00:28:27,273 --> 00:28:28,473
- All right.
- You should take it.

709
00:28:29,283 --> 00:28:31,683
This is blocking it. Go inside a bit.

710
00:28:32,113 --> 00:28:33,652
- A bit to the back.
- What should viewers expect...

711
00:28:33,653 --> 00:28:35,252
- to see in this drama?
- Don't show your face.

712
00:28:35,253 --> 00:28:36,923
(Pushing the older bestie for the perfect shot)

713
00:28:38,823 --> 00:28:41,623
(A top photographer at heart)

714
00:28:43,093 --> 00:28:46,633
(My Star turns toward Kwang Kyu.)

715
00:28:48,193 --> 00:28:49,402
- Did you take it?
- Yes.

716
00:28:49,403 --> 00:28:51,063
Chang Wook looked this way just now.

717
00:28:51,703 --> 00:28:52,973
- Did you miss that?
- I didn't get that.

718
00:28:53,473 --> 00:28:55,572
(Goodness)

719
00:28:55,573 --> 00:28:59,173
What charm does "Cho Won" played by Ji Chang Wook have?

720
00:28:59,613 --> 00:29:02,572
He shows his fashionista side...

721
00:29:02,573 --> 00:29:03,913
Oh, the fashionista in Joseon?

722
00:29:04,113 --> 00:29:06,982
(He seemed nervous, but he's doing great.)

723
00:29:06,983 --> 00:29:08,252
- Look up some articles...
- From now on,

724
00:29:08,253 --> 00:29:09,782
- about Chang Wook.
- let's find out the secret...

725
00:29:09,783 --> 00:29:11,783
(He should just do it himself.)

726
00:29:12,923 --> 00:29:16,523
(Checking his latest news articles in real time)

727
00:29:18,463 --> 00:29:21,393
(Nana)

728
00:29:24,703 --> 00:29:27,433
(Nana again)

729
00:29:29,133 --> 00:29:31,473
(Nana once again)

730
00:29:35,013 --> 00:29:36,112
I told you to look up Chang Wook's articles.

731
00:29:36,113 --> 00:29:37,642
Why are you looking at Nana's pictures only?

732
00:29:37,643 --> 00:29:38,842
I'm not.

733
00:29:38,843 --> 00:29:40,313
Seriously.

734
00:29:40,883 --> 00:29:42,652
I was looking at all the pictures.

735
00:29:42,653 --> 00:29:43,883
I looked at all of them.

736
00:29:44,483 --> 00:29:47,093
(Kwang Kyu's honorary My Star Nana)

737
00:29:47,953 --> 00:29:50,492
(He's looking up his real My Star's articles.)

738
00:29:50,493 --> 00:29:53,032
(He found something.)

739
00:29:53,033 --> 00:29:54,562
This is what the article says.

740
00:29:54,563 --> 00:29:56,162
(What is it?)

741
00:29:56,163 --> 00:29:57,433
(Look at this.)

742
00:29:57,733 --> 00:29:58,733
(Bursting into laughter)

743
00:29:58,734 --> 00:29:59,772
This...

744
00:29:59,773 --> 00:30:01,832
Where is this journalist?

745
00:30:01,833 --> 00:30:02,872
Who wrote this?

746
00:30:02,873 --> 00:30:04,373
It's Son Ye Jin and Hyun Bin.

747
00:30:04,543 --> 00:30:05,772
What are we going to do about this?

748
00:30:05,773 --> 00:30:08,942
(Son Ye Jin, Hyun Bin, and Nana)

749
00:30:08,943 --> 00:30:11,182
They wrote Hyun Bin instead of Ji Chang Wook.

750
00:30:11,183 --> 00:30:12,753
(They got the wrong name.)

751
00:30:12,813 --> 00:30:16,083
It must have happened because they're just rushing things here.

752
00:30:18,923 --> 00:30:20,392
(But...)

753
00:30:20,393 --> 00:30:21,552
This journalist...

754
00:30:21,553 --> 00:30:22,962
keeps writing Hyun Bin's name.

755
00:30:22,963 --> 00:30:24,522
(Multiple headlines went up with errors.)

756
00:30:24,523 --> 00:30:25,692
Where is this journalist?

757
00:30:25,693 --> 00:30:28,732
(A new task came up. Find the journalist...)

758
00:30:28,733 --> 00:30:29,802
Look for the journalist.

759
00:30:29,803 --> 00:30:34,033
(and get the headlines corrected.)

760
00:30:35,473 --> 00:30:38,772
(There are 124 attendees. It's like finding a needle in a haystack.)

761
00:30:38,773 --> 00:30:39,873
There are too many people.

762
00:30:40,643 --> 00:30:41,913
How are we going to find this person?

763
00:30:43,283 --> 00:30:47,253
(Overcoming the poor eyesight, he scans with eagle eyes.)

764
00:30:49,883 --> 00:30:51,322
Isn't it that person?

765
00:30:51,323 --> 00:30:53,453
The person in the middle wearing black glasses.

766
00:30:53,823 --> 00:30:55,153
- Wearing a hat?
- There.

767
00:30:55,623 --> 00:30:56,662
Go there.

768
00:30:56,663 --> 00:30:57,793
I don't know.

769
00:30:58,293 --> 00:31:00,962
Is there anyone with the final questions?

770
00:31:00,963 --> 00:31:02,632
We have to hurry. It's the last question.

771
00:31:02,633 --> 00:31:03,763
(It's time for the last question.)

772
00:31:03,963 --> 00:31:05,002
Where is it?

773
00:31:05,003 --> 00:31:06,432
(He heads out first.)

774
00:31:06,433 --> 00:31:07,632
Where should I go?

775
00:31:07,633 --> 00:31:08,673
Go through there.

776
00:31:09,843 --> 00:31:15,373
(He needs to find the journalist before the press conference ends!)

777
00:31:18,913 --> 00:31:20,982
(A desperate dash...)

778
00:31:20,983 --> 00:31:25,483
(by 58-year-old Kwang Kyu, all for My Star)

779
00:31:33,633 --> 00:31:35,433
- Are you a journalist from...
- No.

780
00:31:35,593 --> 00:31:36,662
No?

781
00:31:36,663 --> 00:31:37,763
- No?
- He's over there.

782
00:31:37,903 --> 00:31:38,962
It's not him.

783
00:31:38,963 --> 00:31:40,033
(Live updates)

784
00:31:41,073 --> 00:31:42,332
(A flustered back)

785
00:31:42,333 --> 00:31:43,702
- Where is he?
- The person wearing a hat.

786
00:31:43,703 --> 00:31:45,743
- Over there?
- Yes.

787
00:31:46,173 --> 00:31:49,983
(A golden tip from another journalist)

788
00:31:50,813 --> 00:31:54,483
(He's on his way to meet you.)

789
00:31:56,283 --> 00:31:59,183
(Kwang Kyu)

790
00:32:02,423 --> 00:32:03,523
I saw him.

791
00:32:04,163 --> 00:32:05,193
I saw him.

792
00:32:05,463 --> 00:32:07,193
Actually,

793
00:32:07,263 --> 00:32:09,803
there wasn't anyone walking around there.

794
00:32:09,863 --> 00:32:12,703
But someone kept moving around.

795
00:32:12,903 --> 00:32:14,102
I wondered, "What is he doing?"

796
00:32:14,103 --> 00:32:15,373
(What is he doing?)

797
00:32:15,503 --> 00:32:18,342
"What's happening? What is he doing?"

798
00:32:18,343 --> 00:32:20,073
(What is he doing?)

799
00:32:23,383 --> 00:32:25,312
(He finally meets the journalist who wrote Hyun Bin.)

800
00:32:25,313 --> 00:32:26,652
(Showing him)

801
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:27,783
Hyun Bin...

802
00:32:27,883 --> 00:32:29,983
- I'll correct them.
- Right.

803
00:32:30,723 --> 00:32:36,053
(Kwang Kyu successfully requests the correction of the articles.)

804
00:32:36,863 --> 00:32:39,422
(Crouching)

805
00:32:39,423 --> 00:32:43,433
(The rough road back after completing the mission)

806
00:32:44,103 --> 00:32:46,062
(Falling)

807
00:32:46,063 --> 00:32:47,972
It wouldn't be nice to draw attention to myself.

808
00:32:47,973 --> 00:32:49,572
I didn't want to cause inconvenience to anyone.

809
00:32:49,573 --> 00:32:52,872
I quietly waddled out.

810
00:32:52,873 --> 00:32:54,343
But you drew attention.

811
00:32:54,373 --> 00:32:55,412
I did?

812
00:32:55,413 --> 00:32:56,583
(I did?)

813
00:32:58,783 --> 00:32:59,852
(Laughing)

814
00:32:59,853 --> 00:33:02,513
(He reaches the final obstacle, the line of cameras.)

815
00:33:03,953 --> 00:33:07,023
It was like going through barbed wire in my military days.

816
00:33:09,793 --> 00:33:10,963
(Panting)

817
00:33:12,593 --> 00:33:13,693
(Panting)

818
00:33:14,333 --> 00:33:15,533
(Panting)

819
00:33:15,793 --> 00:33:16,933
(Panting)

820
00:33:17,763 --> 00:33:20,872
(I made it!)

821
00:33:20,873 --> 00:33:23,243
My joints are hurting everywhere.

822
00:33:25,343 --> 00:33:26,442
I can't rotate it.

823
00:33:26,443 --> 00:33:30,443
(The correction of the article cost him his joints.)

824
00:33:30,783 --> 00:33:32,082
You did a great job.

825
00:33:32,083 --> 00:33:33,253
- I did a great job, right?
- You did.

826
00:33:33,453 --> 00:33:35,612
- Then...
- It would have been trouble.

827
00:33:35,613 --> 00:33:37,123
Can I go home now?

828
00:33:37,953 --> 00:33:40,623
- I'll go home. You carry on.
- No.

829
00:33:41,053 --> 00:33:42,522
It was nice meeting you.

830
00:33:42,523 --> 00:33:44,692
(My Star's press conference ended well...)

831
00:33:44,693 --> 00:33:47,193
(after the correction of the article.)

832
00:33:48,093 --> 00:33:49,093
(Sighing)

833
00:33:49,663 --> 00:33:51,862
(He's still exhausted.)

834
00:33:51,863 --> 00:33:52,972
Great job.

835
00:33:52,973 --> 00:33:54,132
(Great job)

836
00:33:54,133 --> 00:33:55,272
Well done.

837
00:33:55,273 --> 00:33:56,342
Great work.

838
00:33:56,343 --> 00:33:57,673
(Great job)

839
00:33:58,503 --> 00:33:59,772
I could see you so well.

840
00:33:59,773 --> 00:34:00,873
(I could see you so well.)

841
00:34:00,973 --> 00:34:02,142
I'm going...

842
00:34:02,143 --> 00:34:03,842
Do you normally...

843
00:34:03,843 --> 00:34:05,542
watch from the side?

844
00:34:05,543 --> 00:34:06,752
- Of course.
- I was touched...

845
00:34:06,753 --> 00:34:09,782
because they kept watching from start to finish.

846
00:34:09,783 --> 00:34:11,382
We're his managers.

847
00:34:11,383 --> 00:34:14,053
(Showing off nonstop)

848
00:34:15,953 --> 00:34:17,992
(His hands are free.)

849
00:34:17,993 --> 00:34:19,632
- Where did I put the bag?
- That's why...

850
00:34:19,633 --> 00:34:21,032
- Hold on.
- The bag.

851
00:34:21,033 --> 00:34:22,762
(Exclaiming)

852
00:34:22,763 --> 00:34:24,233
Don't worry about him.

853
00:34:24,433 --> 00:34:26,063
How can I not worry about him?

854
00:34:26,163 --> 00:34:27,273
Your bag.

855
00:34:27,973 --> 00:34:29,232
Where did I put your bag?

856
00:34:29,233 --> 00:34:30,843
The bag is missing again.

857
00:34:31,073 --> 00:34:32,172
(The case of My Star's missing bag after his missing tumbler)

858
00:34:32,173 --> 00:34:33,343
Quickly head back.

859
00:34:33,473 --> 00:34:35,173
I'll go and look for the bag.

860
00:34:35,243 --> 00:34:36,483
Were we on the first floor?

861
00:34:36,543 --> 00:34:38,413
- L1 level.
- L1 level.

862
00:34:39,983 --> 00:34:41,683
Goodness.

863
00:34:42,213 --> 00:34:43,922
Just when I thought everything was perfect...

864
00:34:43,923 --> 00:34:45,283
(No wonder things were going so smoothly.)

865
00:34:45,923 --> 00:34:47,092
There it is.

866
00:34:47,093 --> 00:34:48,993
(There it is.)

867
00:34:49,523 --> 00:34:53,263
(He found the bag.)

868
00:34:54,233 --> 00:34:58,833
(He found the journalist and the bag.)

869
00:34:59,673 --> 00:35:02,032
I did my part.

870
00:35:02,033 --> 00:35:03,403
(Heading back to My Star)

871
00:35:04,073 --> 00:35:06,813
(Chang Wook got changed.)

872
00:35:06,913 --> 00:35:09,413
- You should eat.
- You should eat.

873
00:35:09,883 --> 00:35:11,483
You should eat first.

874
00:35:11,683 --> 00:35:12,912
Don't worry about us.

875
00:35:12,913 --> 00:35:13,983
Is this your seat?

876
00:35:14,183 --> 00:35:15,383
Is it this one?

877
00:35:15,653 --> 00:35:19,622
(My Star's Schedule: 12pm, Lunch time)

878
00:35:19,623 --> 00:35:20,693
You should eat.

879
00:35:20,753 --> 00:35:22,223
Okay.

880
00:35:23,493 --> 00:35:27,133
(My Star's brief break...)

881
00:35:27,533 --> 00:35:29,962
(in between a packed schedule of photo ops and interviews)

882
00:35:29,963 --> 00:35:31,063
Goodness.

883
00:35:32,963 --> 00:35:34,202
Is it...

884
00:35:34,203 --> 00:35:35,833
Is it your first press conference of the year?

885
00:35:35,973 --> 00:35:37,172
Me?

886
00:35:37,173 --> 00:35:39,643
Is this my first one this year?

887
00:35:39,773 --> 00:35:41,612
- There was "Colony."
- There was another one, right?

888
00:35:41,613 --> 00:35:43,313
Yes. There was "Colony."

889
00:35:43,383 --> 00:35:44,442
Right.

890
00:35:44,443 --> 00:35:45,542
(3 projects released this year alone.)

891
00:35:45,543 --> 00:35:46,683
That's right.

892
00:35:47,483 --> 00:35:49,923
You did three press conferences in a year?

893
00:35:50,753 --> 00:35:52,452
Me? I kept...

894
00:35:52,453 --> 00:35:55,152
I've worked on a lot of projects.

895
00:35:55,153 --> 00:35:56,252
I did that because...

896
00:35:56,253 --> 00:35:57,892
I think I've been going through...

897
00:35:57,893 --> 00:35:59,762
that period lately.

898
00:35:59,763 --> 00:36:01,693
A period where I want to do many things.

899
00:36:01,793 --> 00:36:02,992
I want to do more things.

900
00:36:02,993 --> 00:36:05,402
You worked with us last October, right?

901
00:36:05,403 --> 00:36:06,702
- That's right.
- Right?

902
00:36:06,703 --> 00:36:08,402
That was a drama called "The Manipulated..."

903
00:36:08,403 --> 00:36:09,703
which I worked on with Kyung Soo.

904
00:36:09,773 --> 00:36:11,202
He found it.

905
00:36:11,203 --> 00:36:12,843
(Clapping)

906
00:36:13,713 --> 00:36:16,543
- Would you like coffee?
- Thank you.

907
00:36:16,743 --> 00:36:17,983
Have something to eat.

908
00:36:18,013 --> 00:36:19,183
Lunch?

909
00:36:19,513 --> 00:36:20,553
Is our lunch here?

910
00:36:21,083 --> 00:36:22,182
He's...

911
00:36:22,183 --> 00:36:23,782
(A simple man who lights up at the word "food.")

912
00:36:23,783 --> 00:36:25,483
Goodness.

913
00:36:25,583 --> 00:36:26,693
First...

914
00:36:27,423 --> 00:36:29,762
During the press conference earlier,

915
00:36:29,763 --> 00:36:30,763
Yes.

916
00:36:31,423 --> 00:36:35,532
Kwang Kyu kept moving around at the very front.

917
00:36:35,533 --> 00:36:37,133
- Yes.
- So...

918
00:36:37,303 --> 00:36:40,133
Seo Jin was watching from the side.

919
00:36:40,373 --> 00:36:41,433
It was reassuring.

920
00:36:42,473 --> 00:36:44,073
How did I do today?

921
00:36:44,973 --> 00:36:46,642
Today...

922
00:36:46,643 --> 00:36:49,213
Overall, I think everything went smoothly...

923
00:36:49,373 --> 00:36:51,682
and without any issues.

924
00:36:51,683 --> 00:36:53,682
- What kind of...
- What?

925
00:36:53,683 --> 00:36:55,213
(In what way were there no issues?)

926
00:36:55,353 --> 00:36:56,883
There was an issue!

927
00:36:57,523 --> 00:37:00,193
There was an issue...

928
00:37:00,693 --> 00:37:02,293
What kind of issue was it?

929
00:37:02,493 --> 00:37:05,022
Instead of Ji Chang Wook, the world star,

930
00:37:05,023 --> 00:37:07,032
- Yes.
- they kept using Hyun Bin's name.

931
00:37:07,033 --> 00:37:09,132
- They kept posting such articles.
- Because of Son Ye Jin.

932
00:37:09,133 --> 00:37:11,663
For example, it went like this.

933
00:37:12,203 --> 00:37:13,432
("The Scandal," starring Son Ye Jin, Hyun Bin, and Nana, is a romance?)

934
00:37:13,433 --> 00:37:14,473
Like that.

935
00:37:15,373 --> 00:37:17,573
- We found the journalist...
- Yes.

936
00:37:18,003 --> 00:37:19,243
and asked for a correction.

937
00:37:19,643 --> 00:37:21,872
That was why he came in...

938
00:37:21,873 --> 00:37:23,072
and talked to that person.

939
00:37:23,073 --> 00:37:24,213
- Right.
- You saw that?

940
00:37:24,643 --> 00:37:26,553
Someone kept walking around,

941
00:37:26,883 --> 00:37:28,513
so I looked at him. It was Kwang Kyu...

942
00:37:28,883 --> 00:37:31,152
talking to a journalist about something.

943
00:37:31,153 --> 00:37:33,083
So I was wondering what it was about.

944
00:37:33,353 --> 00:37:36,323
I had no idea it would be about that. I'm so grateful.

945
00:37:36,723 --> 00:37:39,262
- We took care of it smoothly.
- Thank you.

946
00:37:39,263 --> 00:37:43,032
He kept getting your name wrong...

947
00:37:43,033 --> 00:37:45,263
in many articles.

948
00:37:45,963 --> 00:37:47,602
(Let's eat now.)

949
00:37:47,603 --> 00:37:49,172
- Let's eat.
- Thank you for the food.

950
00:37:49,173 --> 00:37:50,203
Today...

951
00:37:50,973 --> 00:37:55,173
(He only gets 50 minutes to eat.)

952
00:37:55,543 --> 00:37:56,913
What will I be doing after lunch?

953
00:37:57,983 --> 00:37:59,043
After lunch?

954
00:38:00,013 --> 00:38:01,882
You have an interview.

955
00:38:01,883 --> 00:38:03,452
An interview.

956
00:38:03,453 --> 00:38:05,852
(Seo Jin already memorized the schedule.)

957
00:38:05,853 --> 00:38:06,853
But...

958
00:38:06,854 --> 00:38:07,953
(But...)

959
00:38:08,193 --> 00:38:10,923
working from 9am to 6pm is a bit...

960
00:38:11,823 --> 00:38:13,332
Are other press conferences like this too?

961
00:38:13,333 --> 00:38:14,393
Yes.

962
00:38:14,833 --> 00:38:17,362
Since there aren't many chances to gather up like this,

963
00:38:17,363 --> 00:38:20,403
we keep doing interviews when we can gather them.

964
00:38:20,803 --> 00:38:23,472
I've never seen one that's so long.

965
00:38:23,473 --> 00:38:25,073
(It would be really tiresome.)

966
00:38:28,073 --> 00:38:30,413
You kept wandering around Son Ye Jin...

967
00:38:31,983 --> 00:38:34,753
and Nana.

968
00:38:35,253 --> 00:38:36,313
Who?

969
00:38:37,253 --> 00:38:38,783
What are you talking about?

970
00:38:39,153 --> 00:38:41,253
I kept taking pictures of you.

971
00:38:41,893 --> 00:38:44,323
You took the fan to Nana.

972
00:38:45,093 --> 00:38:48,363
You took a water bottle to Ye Jin.

973
00:38:48,493 --> 00:38:50,202
- What?
- Honey?

974
00:38:50,203 --> 00:38:51,763
He gave her honey? Who?

975
00:38:52,233 --> 00:38:54,072
- You gave it to her.
- My honey?

976
00:38:54,073 --> 00:38:55,133
That's right.

977
00:38:56,433 --> 00:38:58,442
I didn't give her the honey. It was Seo Jin.

978
00:38:58,443 --> 00:38:59,443
No.

979
00:38:59,443 --> 00:39:00,443
(My Star's mood is starting to drop.)

980
00:39:00,444 --> 00:39:01,513
I didn't give it to her.

981
00:39:01,573 --> 00:39:03,113
This is how it feels.

982
00:39:05,313 --> 00:39:07,252
She asked for one and I didn't give her.

983
00:39:07,253 --> 00:39:09,183
I don't mind them...

984
00:39:09,553 --> 00:39:11,222
giving my things to others...

985
00:39:11,223 --> 00:39:14,652
because they do that in good will.

986
00:39:14,653 --> 00:39:17,793
It's fine since she needs it.

987
00:39:18,823 --> 00:39:20,292
But I'm a bit disappointed because they didn't do...

988
00:39:20,293 --> 00:39:21,792
any of that for me.

989
00:39:21,793 --> 00:39:25,362
(They didn't do any of that for me.)

990
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:26,432
(This is bad.)

991
00:39:26,433 --> 00:39:28,932
It was in the bag.

992
00:39:28,933 --> 00:39:30,342
I didn't give it to her when she asked for one.

993
00:39:30,343 --> 00:39:31,472
(Ye Jin asked for it, but he didn't give her.)

994
00:39:31,473 --> 00:39:32,872
(I asked for it?)

995
00:39:32,873 --> 00:39:33,873
- Hey.
- Yes?

996
00:39:34,573 --> 00:39:36,072
How did she know you had honey?

997
00:39:36,073 --> 00:39:39,013
Ye Jin didn't want it, but you kept insisting.

998
00:39:39,443 --> 00:39:41,152
What are you talking about? She asked for it and I refused.

999
00:39:41,153 --> 00:39:43,423
- Ye Jin asked for it?
- She knew there was honey.

1000
00:39:43,683 --> 00:39:45,122
How did she know I had honey?

1001
00:39:45,123 --> 00:39:46,722
I guess she knows that you normally carry honey.

1002
00:39:46,723 --> 00:39:48,753
I'm getting confused since he's so confident.

1003
00:39:49,053 --> 00:39:51,923
- No way.
- I didn't give it to her.

1004
00:39:52,123 --> 00:39:53,262
You gave it to her.

1005
00:39:53,263 --> 00:39:55,193
- I didn't.
- Goodness.

1006
00:39:55,333 --> 00:39:57,302
Where is it?

1007
00:39:57,303 --> 00:39:58,732
You did offer her.

1008
00:39:58,733 --> 00:40:01,972
I didn't offer her. I just said, "There's honey. Do you want one?"

1009
00:40:01,973 --> 00:40:03,502
That's what...

1010
00:40:03,503 --> 00:40:05,203
- This...
- Let's check the tapes.

1011
00:40:05,543 --> 00:40:07,012
Let's check the tapes.

1012
00:40:07,013 --> 00:40:08,472
How much will you bet?

1013
00:40:08,473 --> 00:40:10,982
- What?
- I can bet my whole fortune.

1014
00:40:10,983 --> 00:40:12,642
(He's scared.)

1015
00:40:12,643 --> 00:40:14,513
- That's big.
- How much do you have?

1016
00:40:14,583 --> 00:40:15,613
Bet all of it.

1017
00:40:16,313 --> 00:40:17,922
I didn't even know there was honey.

1018
00:40:17,923 --> 00:40:19,222
(He's never even seen the honey.)

1019
00:40:19,223 --> 00:40:22,922
Even if I keep feeling hurt,

1020
00:40:22,923 --> 00:40:23,923
(My Star isn't getting anything out of it.)

1021
00:40:23,924 --> 00:40:26,063
they're not going to give me honey.

1022
00:40:26,193 --> 00:40:27,432
Is there really honey?

1023
00:40:27,433 --> 00:40:29,693
(Let me see it.)

1024
00:40:30,863 --> 00:40:32,032
My Star.

1025
00:40:32,033 --> 00:40:33,033
(The honey his real manager packed for him)

1026
00:40:33,133 --> 00:40:34,232
Have some honey.

1027
00:40:34,233 --> 00:40:37,143
(Getting honey before Chuseok just because he asked)

1028
00:40:38,503 --> 00:40:39,703
It's really not nice.

1029
00:40:42,173 --> 00:40:45,913
(The secretaries who enjoyed the honey are not nice.)

1030
00:40:46,213 --> 00:40:49,712
I said that when you were holding the fan.

1031
00:40:49,713 --> 00:40:50,783
How would you know that?

1032
00:40:51,353 --> 00:40:52,553
That's why...

1033
00:40:52,883 --> 00:40:53,892
So that's why you went to Nana...

1034
00:40:53,893 --> 00:40:55,293
and told her you should have a meal together sometime.

1035
00:40:55,423 --> 00:40:56,792
Kwang Kyu...

1036
00:40:56,793 --> 00:40:58,723
(Did you see that?)

1037
00:40:58,993 --> 00:41:00,563
He didn't ask me that.

1038
00:41:02,333 --> 00:41:03,502
I mean...

1039
00:41:03,503 --> 00:41:05,602
(Please explain that.)

1040
00:41:05,603 --> 00:41:06,733
I mean...

1041
00:41:07,133 --> 00:41:09,232
When did you ask to grab a meal? This month?

1042
00:41:09,233 --> 00:41:10,773
No.

1043
00:41:10,903 --> 00:41:12,272
- Were you trying to make plans?
- No.

1044
00:41:12,273 --> 00:41:14,173
I asked her if she'd like to join us...

1045
00:41:14,473 --> 00:41:17,043
and Ji Chang Wook for a packed lunch.

1046
00:41:17,743 --> 00:41:19,413
She seemed to have plans.

1047
00:41:20,883 --> 00:41:22,852
You were rejected?

1048
00:41:22,853 --> 00:41:24,722
(That's what we call being rejected.)

1049
00:41:24,723 --> 00:41:28,723
(Facing the reality he tried to ignore)

1050
00:41:28,993 --> 00:41:31,123
- I thought we'd eat with Nana.
- Charge that fan.

1051
00:41:31,193 --> 00:41:33,763
It feels like it wouldn't work because you used it so much.

1052
00:41:33,933 --> 00:41:35,262
It works.

1053
00:41:35,263 --> 00:41:36,392
- This...
- You used it on Nana...

1054
00:41:36,393 --> 00:41:37,503
for like 30 minutes.

1055
00:41:37,963 --> 00:41:40,203
(Crying)

1056
00:41:40,733 --> 00:41:43,202
It's not strong enough.

1057
00:41:43,203 --> 00:41:46,173
(The air gun is still alive.)

1058
00:41:46,373 --> 00:41:49,843
Even his fan is different because he's a global actor.

1059
00:41:50,083 --> 00:41:51,242
Was this given to you as a gift?

1060
00:41:51,243 --> 00:41:52,383
No. I bought it.

1061
00:41:52,983 --> 00:41:54,483
Ji Hyun...

1062
00:41:54,983 --> 00:41:56,453
Her manager...

1063
00:41:56,653 --> 00:41:57,722
Who's Ji Hyun?

1064
00:41:57,723 --> 00:41:59,522
Jun Ji Hyun.

1065
00:41:59,523 --> 00:42:00,652
Your favourite Jun Ji Hyun.

1066
00:42:00,653 --> 00:42:02,952
Jun Ji Hyun?

1067
00:42:02,953 --> 00:42:04,462
Of course.

1068
00:42:04,463 --> 00:42:05,892
- Did you ever work with her?
- Of course.

1069
00:42:05,893 --> 00:42:07,362
We worked on "Windstruck" together.

1070
00:42:07,363 --> 00:42:08,432
(A character who gets overpowered by Jun Ji Hyun)

1071
00:42:08,433 --> 00:42:10,532
I remember getting slapped by Jun Ji Hyun.

1072
00:42:10,533 --> 00:42:12,733
(They were close enough that he even got slapped by her.)

1073
00:42:12,933 --> 00:42:14,973
Then when we're promoting "HumanXGumiho..."

1074
00:42:15,533 --> 00:42:18,043
He'll be working on a drama with Jun Ji Hyun.

1075
00:42:18,243 --> 00:42:19,272
- He is currently working on it.
- You are?

1076
00:42:19,273 --> 00:42:20,342
- Yes.
- He's working on it.

1077
00:42:20,343 --> 00:42:22,572
It will be released next year.

1078
00:42:22,573 --> 00:42:24,413
- We have to promote that.
- Right.

1079
00:42:24,513 --> 00:42:27,013
Let's have Chang Wook as a permanent member.

1080
00:42:28,083 --> 00:42:29,752
As a promotion day.

1081
00:42:29,753 --> 00:42:31,222
You'll always be with us on promotion days.

1082
00:42:31,223 --> 00:42:32,253
(Sighing)

1083
00:42:33,653 --> 00:42:35,823
I wasn't sighing because of that.

1084
00:42:36,223 --> 00:42:39,022
That's not what I meant. These days,

1085
00:42:39,023 --> 00:42:41,932
I have so many things to do that I just sigh without realising.

1086
00:42:41,933 --> 00:42:43,363
- Yes.
- Try to work a little less.

1087
00:42:45,963 --> 00:42:48,072
I'm thinking of leaving behind the honey next time.

1088
00:42:48,073 --> 00:42:49,733
(We'll give you honey when you come, Jun Ji Hyun.)

1089
00:42:50,203 --> 00:42:51,472
How many months did you work on this?

1090
00:42:51,473 --> 00:42:53,143
(Back to talking about the drama)

1091
00:42:53,613 --> 00:42:55,713
It's been more than six months.

1092
00:42:55,973 --> 00:42:56,982
That was a long shoot.

1093
00:42:56,983 --> 00:42:58,043
(My Star filmed over 6 months.)

1094
00:42:58,183 --> 00:42:59,812
Even with the post-production...

1095
00:42:59,813 --> 00:43:02,583
The director is quite meticulous,

1096
00:43:02,853 --> 00:43:04,582
so he must have worked a lot on the post-production.

1097
00:43:04,583 --> 00:43:06,552
- We re-recorded the dialogue...
- See?

1098
00:43:06,553 --> 00:43:08,752
for almost 20 hours.

1099
00:43:08,753 --> 00:43:09,952
(Nearly 20 hours per actor)

1100
00:43:09,953 --> 00:43:10,992
Just to re-record the dialogue.

1101
00:43:10,993 --> 00:43:12,862
That would have been everything from start to end.

1102
00:43:12,863 --> 00:43:13,933
That's right.

1103
00:43:14,733 --> 00:43:16,463
I worked on "Modern Boy" for a brief time.

1104
00:43:16,793 --> 00:43:19,062
Even though all the scenes were edited out,

1105
00:43:19,063 --> 00:43:20,573
I dubbed...

1106
00:43:21,033 --> 00:43:22,973
You were completely edited out? You didn't appear?

1107
00:43:23,473 --> 00:43:24,642
I don't think I appeared.

1108
00:43:24,643 --> 00:43:26,972
(Even the dubbed voice was edited out.)

1109
00:43:26,973 --> 00:43:28,073
Not even one scene?

1110
00:43:28,143 --> 00:43:30,242
I couldn't find myself.

1111
00:43:30,243 --> 00:43:31,342
Not even one scene?

1112
00:43:31,343 --> 00:43:33,042
They edited so many scenes out.

1113
00:43:33,043 --> 00:43:34,683
(He failed to leave because of the bag.)

1114
00:43:35,183 --> 00:43:37,353
The director kept avoiding my eyes.

1115
00:43:37,853 --> 00:43:39,323
- He avoided mine as well.
- What?

1116
00:43:39,383 --> 00:43:40,552
Why did he avoid your eyes?

1117
00:43:40,553 --> 00:43:42,353
I auditioned for "Happy End" and failed.

1118
00:43:43,423 --> 00:43:45,592
We share a common pain.

1119
00:43:45,593 --> 00:43:47,293
- We share a common pain.
- Don't put me there.

1120
00:43:48,363 --> 00:43:49,932
(The man shows up on his own.)

1121
00:43:49,933 --> 00:43:51,063
Really?

1122
00:43:51,763 --> 00:43:53,632
- Great work today.
- Are you leaving?

1123
00:43:53,633 --> 00:43:54,672
(Director Jung Ji Woo came to greet them.)

1124
00:43:54,673 --> 00:43:57,372
- Yes. Great work.
- See you later.

1125
00:43:57,373 --> 00:43:59,102
Have a cup of coffee before you go.

1126
00:43:59,103 --> 00:44:01,042
- Pardon?
- Yes. Have a cup of coffee.

1127
00:44:01,043 --> 00:44:03,142
Why are you avoiding Kwang Kyu?

1128
00:44:03,143 --> 00:44:04,583
I heard you completely edited him out.

1129
00:44:04,783 --> 00:44:06,983
- No...
- Where are you going?

1130
00:44:07,783 --> 00:44:10,283
(Kwang Kyu persistently goes after him.)

1131
00:44:10,453 --> 00:44:12,782
(Struggling)

1132
00:44:12,783 --> 00:44:15,322
(He successfully escaped.)

1133
00:44:15,323 --> 00:44:17,292
He really ran away.

1134
00:44:17,293 --> 00:44:19,563
Why did you mention that?

1135
00:44:19,863 --> 00:44:22,232
He wouldn't call me next time.

1136
00:44:22,233 --> 00:44:24,033
(While Victims 1 and 2 are feeling disappointed...)

1137
00:44:24,633 --> 00:44:25,662
(He got changed.)

1138
00:44:25,663 --> 00:44:27,633
Chang Wook. Have some coffee.

1139
00:44:27,803 --> 00:44:30,803
I want some coffee.

1140
00:44:31,243 --> 00:44:32,873
That's right.

1141
00:44:33,503 --> 00:44:35,642
Why are we clinking our glasses?

1142
00:44:35,643 --> 00:44:36,742
(My Star has to do interviews from now on.)

1143
00:44:36,743 --> 00:44:38,243
Cheers.

1144
00:44:38,783 --> 00:44:40,142
- To cheer you up.
- Hey.

1145
00:44:40,143 --> 00:44:41,653
You get no time to rest.

1146
00:44:42,253 --> 00:44:43,553
This doesn't have sugar.

1147
00:44:43,823 --> 00:44:46,553
(Barista Kwang Kyu feels proud too.)

1148
00:44:47,553 --> 00:44:50,323
(When things are busy and hectic,)

1149
00:44:50,463 --> 00:44:53,223
(caffeine is the best.)

1150
00:44:54,933 --> 00:44:56,462
You have to get going now.

1151
00:44:56,463 --> 00:44:59,133
(Back to work after a sweet break)

1152
00:44:59,333 --> 00:45:00,902
(My Star's Schedule)

1153
00:45:00,903 --> 00:45:02,272
(1pm, Interview shoot 1)

1154
00:45:02,273 --> 00:45:06,773
(Private Shoot)

1155
00:45:07,743 --> 00:45:09,573
We shouldn't be filming this, right?

1156
00:45:11,513 --> 00:45:13,852
Let's stay in our room.

1157
00:45:13,853 --> 00:45:14,913
(Heading to the waiting room due to a private interview issue)

1158
00:45:17,453 --> 00:45:21,153
Why does he have interviews nonstop?

1159
00:45:23,823 --> 00:45:26,423
(My Star went into a 3-hour interview.)

1160
00:45:27,863 --> 00:45:31,803
(While My Star is in his private interview...)

1161
00:45:33,003 --> 00:45:37,173
(They go outside with their hands full.)

1162
00:45:39,243 --> 00:45:41,142
- This is Cheonggyecheon Stream.
- What?

1163
00:45:41,143 --> 00:45:42,313
It's Cheonggyecheon Stream.

1164
00:45:43,173 --> 00:45:44,413
Is it the Cheonggyecheon Stream flowing below?

1165
00:45:44,513 --> 00:45:46,682
- That's right.
- It's Cheonggyecheon Stream.

1166
00:45:46,683 --> 00:45:48,113
(They see Cheonggyecheon Stream as soon as they step out.)

1167
00:45:48,553 --> 00:45:50,053
Shall we just walk along Cheonggyecheon Stream?

1168
00:45:51,383 --> 00:45:53,252
- You've never been to it, right?
- Right.

1169
00:45:53,253 --> 00:45:56,553
Look at this city boy.

1170
00:45:57,393 --> 00:45:59,293
I've been to Cheonggyecheon Stream like two times.

1171
00:46:01,963 --> 00:46:03,062
I'm in trouble.

1172
00:46:03,063 --> 00:46:04,102
(What are those?)

1173
00:46:04,103 --> 00:46:05,163
My head feels hot.

1174
00:46:05,303 --> 00:46:08,072
They asked you to promote it to people on the street.

1175
00:46:08,073 --> 00:46:09,772
- What?
- Promote it to the public.

1176
00:46:09,773 --> 00:46:11,372
(The request for street promotion?)

1177
00:46:11,373 --> 00:46:12,773
Are you taking them all?

1178
00:46:12,843 --> 00:46:14,512
- Yes.
- Who's going to carry them?

1179
00:46:14,513 --> 00:46:16,812
On September 18, "The Scandal" will launch at 5pm...

1180
00:46:16,813 --> 00:46:17,842
At 5pm?

1181
00:46:17,843 --> 00:46:18,982
Yes, at 5pm.

1182
00:46:18,983 --> 00:46:21,253
If you walk just a bit, there's Dongdaemun Market.

1183
00:46:22,183 --> 00:46:24,383
If you walk just a bit, there's Dongdaemun Market.

1184
00:46:25,453 --> 00:46:28,723
We can go to Migliore or Doota.

1185
00:46:29,153 --> 00:46:31,662
We can buy clothes for fall...

1186
00:46:31,663 --> 00:46:34,132
and give it out to the store owners.

1187
00:46:34,133 --> 00:46:35,532
- To promote in person?
- Yes.

1188
00:46:35,533 --> 00:46:39,603
(They'll even promote it in person.)

1189
00:46:39,763 --> 00:46:41,172
How are you going to promote it to people from abroad?

1190
00:46:41,173 --> 00:46:42,772
Hi. Nice to meet you.

1191
00:46:42,773 --> 00:46:44,743
Welcome. Come on.

1192
00:46:45,743 --> 00:46:49,773
It's an OTT drama, "The Scandal."

1193
00:46:50,173 --> 00:46:52,042
Yes. May 18.

1194
00:46:52,043 --> 00:46:53,883
(In Korean)

1195
00:46:54,213 --> 00:46:55,312
What?

1196
00:46:55,313 --> 00:46:56,412
- May 18.
- September 18.

1197
00:46:56,413 --> 00:46:57,723
- May 18.
- September.

1198
00:46:57,783 --> 00:46:59,452
- May 18.
- September.

1199
00:46:59,453 --> 00:47:00,692
Oh, September 18.

1200
00:47:00,693 --> 00:47:02,892
Do you know me? Hi. Nice to meet you.

1201
00:47:02,893 --> 00:47:04,262
- Nice to meet you.
- Yes.

1202
00:47:04,263 --> 00:47:05,792
- Welcome to Korea.
- Bye.

1203
00:47:05,793 --> 00:47:09,892
- Thank you. Bye.
- September 18.

1204
00:47:09,893 --> 00:47:12,402
- It starts at 5pm.
- Yes.

1205
00:47:12,403 --> 00:47:13,403
Okay.

1206
00:47:13,404 --> 00:47:16,632
(Leave the English conversation to the Genie.)

1207
00:47:16,633 --> 00:47:18,142
- Okay. Bye.
- Bye.

1208
00:47:18,143 --> 00:47:19,273
(What he knows in English)

1209
00:47:23,413 --> 00:47:25,212
Why don't we promote it to people from abroad?

1210
00:47:25,213 --> 00:47:27,313
- Sounds good.
- What?

1211
00:47:27,553 --> 00:47:30,383
Since it's a global drama, let's promote it to foreigners.

1212
00:47:30,723 --> 00:47:32,082
There are many foreigners in Dongdaemun.

1213
00:47:32,083 --> 00:47:33,383
- That's right.
- Right?

1214
00:47:33,853 --> 00:47:35,553
People from abroad might not know.

1215
00:47:36,053 --> 00:47:38,193
It's only right to promote it to people from abroad.

1216
00:47:38,823 --> 00:47:40,562
I've worked as a salesman for a long time.

1217
00:47:40,563 --> 00:47:41,993
For example, in fashion.

1218
00:47:42,763 --> 00:47:45,163
First of all, you have to be shameless.

1219
00:47:45,703 --> 00:47:46,863
You can't be shy.

1220
00:47:47,033 --> 00:47:48,603
Approach them with confidence.

1221
00:47:48,703 --> 00:47:50,542
Start a conversation with confidence.

1222
00:47:50,543 --> 00:47:52,642
How shameless do you have to be...

1223
00:47:52,643 --> 00:47:54,373
to talk to foreigners in Korean?

1224
00:47:55,273 --> 00:47:57,012
That's how shameless you have to be.

1225
00:47:57,013 --> 00:47:59,883
So we can communicate and promote the series.

1226
00:48:00,113 --> 00:48:01,952
That's the spirit you need.

1227
00:48:01,953 --> 00:48:04,022
(The shameless promotion secretary is ready.)

1228
00:48:04,023 --> 00:48:05,323
Anyway, it's too hot.

1229
00:48:09,393 --> 00:48:10,793
It's Cheonggyecheon Stream.

1230
00:48:11,863 --> 00:48:13,562
- It's nice, isn't it?
- Yes.

1231
00:48:13,563 --> 00:48:14,593
(The Seoul hillbilly in Cheonggyecheon Stream)

1232
00:48:15,093 --> 00:48:16,493
(Intrigued)

1233
00:48:20,433 --> 00:48:21,503
- Kwang Kyu.
- Yes?

1234
00:48:21,773 --> 00:48:23,633
That carp is so big.

1235
00:48:23,703 --> 00:48:26,002
- Oh, that's huge.
- Right?

1236
00:48:26,003 --> 00:48:27,312
I didn't know it could get that big.

1237
00:48:27,313 --> 00:48:28,413
Are there supposed to be carp?

1238
00:48:29,113 --> 00:48:30,782
(Taking a walk in Cheonggyecheon Stream)

1239
00:48:30,783 --> 00:48:31,783
That's big.

1240
00:48:32,843 --> 00:48:35,013
That's really big. Amazing.

1241
00:48:38,783 --> 00:48:41,393
I used to come here a lot 20 years ago.

1242
00:48:44,893 --> 00:48:46,822
Check out the cloud in the sky.

1243
00:48:46,823 --> 00:48:48,163
It looks strange.

1244
00:48:49,833 --> 00:48:51,032
Hey, isn't that a rainbow?

1245
00:48:51,033 --> 00:48:53,433
(Getting sentimental)

1246
00:48:53,663 --> 00:48:55,172
How can there be a rainbow without rain?

1247
00:48:55,173 --> 00:48:56,933
Up there. Look.

1248
00:48:57,703 --> 00:49:00,103
(Seo Jin's being too realistic.)

1249
00:49:00,973 --> 00:49:02,012
It's nice.

1250
00:49:02,013 --> 00:49:03,913
How can you be so amazed...

1251
00:49:04,143 --> 00:49:06,443
by Dongdaemun when you live in Seoul?

1252
00:49:07,583 --> 00:49:09,182
- It...
- What?

1253
00:49:09,183 --> 00:49:11,683
It'd be nice to check out Cheonggyecheon Stream.

1254
00:49:13,453 --> 00:49:15,423
Hello.

1255
00:49:16,793 --> 00:49:18,492
I'm a fan of My Genie Secretary.

1256
00:49:18,493 --> 00:49:19,893
Thank you.

1257
00:49:20,693 --> 00:49:22,892
I should give her one...

1258
00:49:22,893 --> 00:49:24,063
since she says she's a fan.

1259
00:49:25,633 --> 00:49:28,602
On OTT on May 18.

1260
00:49:28,603 --> 00:49:31,172
- "The Scandal" at 5pm.
- Thank you.

1261
00:49:31,173 --> 00:49:32,473
Thank you.

1262
00:49:32,603 --> 00:49:34,072
Kwang Kyu, it's September.

1263
00:49:34,073 --> 00:49:36,472
September 18. I keep saying May.

1264
00:49:36,473 --> 00:49:37,683
It's this month.

1265
00:49:38,783 --> 00:49:39,843
It's at 5pm, right?

1266
00:49:40,513 --> 00:49:43,453
(On September 18, "The Scandal" will launch at 5pm.)

1267
00:49:44,183 --> 00:49:45,652
Next Friday.

1268
00:49:45,653 --> 00:49:46,653
(He's shameless, but he doesn't have a good memory.)

1269
00:49:49,323 --> 00:49:51,822
Kids.

1270
00:49:51,823 --> 00:49:52,962
- Hello.
- Hello.

1271
00:49:52,963 --> 00:49:54,533
- Here you are.
- Thank you.

1272
00:49:54,763 --> 00:49:56,932
- Read it out loud.
- "The Scandal."

1273
00:49:56,933 --> 00:49:58,202
- On OTT.
- On OTT.

1274
00:49:58,203 --> 00:49:59,462
Again. Go.

1275
00:49:59,463 --> 00:50:00,932
- "The Scandal" on OTT.
- "The Scandal" on OTT.

1276
00:50:00,933 --> 00:50:03,272
- Good job.
- Thank you.

1277
00:50:03,273 --> 00:50:06,672
But it's R-rated.

1278
00:50:06,673 --> 00:50:08,672
Hey. Give it back.

1279
00:50:08,673 --> 00:50:10,613
- It's...
- It's okay. Give it to them.

1280
00:50:11,013 --> 00:50:12,013
Okay.

1281
00:50:12,643 --> 00:50:14,982
Anyway, tell your parents.

1282
00:50:14,983 --> 00:50:16,252
- Okay.
- "The Scandal."

1283
00:50:16,253 --> 00:50:17,482
What does your father do?

1284
00:50:17,483 --> 00:50:19,083
(Being fan-friendly)

1285
00:50:19,423 --> 00:50:20,592
Okay. Bye.

1286
00:50:20,593 --> 00:50:22,592
- Say he's a gang.
- Okay.

1287
00:50:22,593 --> 00:50:24,862
- Bye.
- Bye.

1288
00:50:24,863 --> 00:50:26,362
- Hey.
- Let's go inside.

1289
00:50:26,363 --> 00:50:27,363
Is it R-rated?

1290
00:50:27,733 --> 00:50:28,733
I guess so.

1291
00:50:29,993 --> 00:50:31,663
Do we need to get permission to film inside?

1292
00:50:32,333 --> 00:50:33,532
Do you have any connection here?

1293
00:50:33,533 --> 00:50:34,672
I know the chairman.

1294
00:50:34,673 --> 00:50:36,332
Can you talk to the chairman?

1295
00:50:36,333 --> 00:50:37,802
(The Young Master is new to Dongdaemun,)

1296
00:50:37,803 --> 00:50:38,903
(but he knows the chairman.)

1297
00:50:39,573 --> 00:50:42,143
I've met the chairman before too.

1298
00:50:43,643 --> 00:50:46,843
(Filmed with the permission in a hurry)

1299
00:50:49,353 --> 00:50:51,553
- It's nice. It's so nice.
- What?

1300
00:50:52,183 --> 00:50:53,423
It's changed so much.

1301
00:50:54,623 --> 00:50:55,953
It's quite different from the past.

1302
00:50:57,823 --> 00:51:00,993
(The building changed a lot compared to 30 years ago.)

1303
00:51:02,463 --> 00:51:03,463
(Spotting a foreigner)

1304
00:51:03,464 --> 00:51:04,603
There's a foreigner.

1305
00:51:06,433 --> 00:51:08,733
- Hi. Hello.
- Hello.

1306
00:51:09,933 --> 00:51:13,042
It's the OTT series. Understand?

1307
00:51:13,043 --> 00:51:14,343
Yes.

1308
00:51:14,743 --> 00:51:16,913
Saturday, September 18...

1309
00:51:17,013 --> 00:51:18,782
Saturday, September 18...

1310
00:51:18,783 --> 00:51:19,783
